1
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:10,279
Greetings to everyone. We offer our words of salutation
to our preceptors, and to their preceptors.

2
00:00:13,759 --> 00:00:21,680
May the glorious Venkatanatha, the lion among poets
and logicians, and the revered teacher of Vedanta, ever reside in my heart [2].

3
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:26,960
Salutations to that Ramanuja, the supreme yogi...

4
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:36,079
...who cooled the inner fever of the Vedas, Smritis, and Sutras.
Salutations again and again to Yamunacharya [1].

5
00:00:36,079 --> 00:00:41,760
Salutations to Nathamuni, salutations to Shatakopa,
salutations to the glorious Sriman Narayana.

6
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:48,920
Here, to me, in myself...

7
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:55,440
My respectful salutations to the elders of this Brahmana...

8
00:00:55,440 --> 00:01:02,160
...Sabha, who have given me the opportunity to speak on a topic
that inspires great enthusiasm in me. I am now...

9
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:05,160
...primarily...

10
00:01:05,519 --> 00:01:11,439
...going to speak briefly about the philosophy (Darshana)
of Ramanujacharya. The objective here is...

11
00:01:11,439 --> 00:01:18,400
...that many people hold bizarre misconceptions about him.
To offer a...

12
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:23,439
...clarification on those, and then highlight his unique
significance, specifically in history...

13
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:28,400
...and what makes him distinct. That is my sole purpose.
In this regard, first...

14
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:35,640
...concerning our three great Acharyas...

15
00:01:35,759 --> 00:01:38,759
Is it not audible?

16
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:45,880
Now?

17
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:57,040
These three Acharyas are highly inspiring to us
because all three of them...

18
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:02,960
...went in search of the ultimate truth. Their...

19
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:08,959
...intent was identical: "I must know Brahman,
I must realize the Supreme Self, the nature of the Atman..."

20
00:02:08,959 --> 00:02:13,599
...such was the truth they set out to seek through intense search.

21
00:02:13,599 --> 00:02:20,000
The pramanas available to them were personal experience,
the words of elders, and the Vedas. Utilizing these...

22
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,360
...they endeavored to attain this truth.
For that reason alone, they...

23
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:30,239
...are all three worthy of reverence by all believers (astikas).

24
00:02:30,239 --> 00:02:36,640
There may be differences in the degree of their success, yet the...

25
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:44,319
...effort they put in was equal. Now, whenever we speak
about any subject, we must consider...

26
00:02:44,319 --> 00:02:49,760
...what the pramana (authority) is. Just because some book
is published by our monastery, which...

27
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:56,000
...says so, or because our grandmother narrated such a story—
that is one kind of claim. But beyond that, there are...

28
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,400
...stone inscriptions, which cannot be hidden by anyone, and
which anyone can verify. That is a reliable pramana.

29
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:10,720
Another strong authority is the very books that these Acharyas
themselves wrote, or spoke and had recorded...

30
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:18,080
...the texts they left behind. These constitute
another class of authoritative pramanas.

31
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:26,560
In this lecture, I will rely primarily on these strong,
authoritative pramanas...

32
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:34,000
...to present my arguments. What often happens is that,
many times, people take legends...

33
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:40,599
...and exaggerations, and present them as historical fact...

34
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:48,480
...speaking untruths about our Acharyas and their traditions.
For neutral observers...

35
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:56,799
...who do not belong to any specific monastery, and who look
at things with an open, questioning mind...

36
00:03:56,799 --> 00:04:01,519
...I will present these topics, relying solely on verifiable evidence.

37
00:04:01,519 --> 00:04:10,000
First, let us look at what naturally and simply comes
to people's minds regarding Ramanuja...

38
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:15,040
...which is that he was a deeply warm-hearted soul, entirely absorbed...

39
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:20,320
...in the contemplation of the Divine.
This is the prevailing sentiment that everyone shares.

40
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:26,320
This is highly acceptable and is certainly not incorrect.
However, based on this...

41
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:32,400
...and relying on it, there are several misconceptions about what
kind of person he was. For instance...

42
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:35,840
...for example...

43
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:41,199
...I will elaborate with an example. Let us begin here:
he was compassionate, and...

44
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:49,440
...deeply absorbed in the experience of the Supreme Self,
in the realization of the inner soul.

45
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:55,360
When his mind and heart were filled with this experience...

46
00:04:55,360 --> 00:05:01,360
...and overflowed, we must ask: how did he act?

47
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:06,479
Was his behavior contrary to the scriptures (Shastras),
or was it aligned with them?

48
00:05:06,479 --> 00:05:13,600
This is an important question. For example, several
modern portrayals of Ramanuja exist...

49
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:21,120
...and many of these portrayals depict him climbing a temple tower...

50
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:28,240
...to loudly broadcast the secret mantra he had received.

51
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:34,320
But this is false. He would never, even in his dreams,
violate the scriptures or commit guru-droha (betray his preceptor).

52
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:37,840
Such an act is out of character.

53
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:42,400
This narrative stems from exaggerations found...

54
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:48,960
...in highly recent, modern texts, which speakers utilize because...

55
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:54,080
...it sounds attractive to the masses. But it is not the historical
truth. That is one misconception. Another...

56
00:05:54,080 --> 00:06:00,639
...misunderstanding is that, in matters of caste and varna,
he acted completely...

57
00:06:00,639 --> 00:06:06,160
...beyond scriptural limits. There is a "Statue of Equality"...

58
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:10,240
...erected near Hyderabad, Telangana, which is a massive monument.

59
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:15,759
Initially, on their website and in their discourses...

60
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:22,160
...such exaggerations were present. However, we must carefully
understand this...

61
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:29,520
Ramanuja was so deeply immersed in the realization of the Divine
that he would never take a single step...

62
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:34,240
...against the command of the Supreme Lord.

63
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:40,080
How do we know the Lord's command? He does not...

64
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:44,000
...directly come and speak to us; rather, He has left behind
the scriptures (Shastras) for us.

65
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:49,840
Ramanuja firmly believed that we must ascertain the Lord's intent
through the Shastras. Accordingly...

66
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:58,319
...he conducted himself strictly. One can say that during his time,
certain social practices...

67
00:06:58,319 --> 00:07:01,759
...masquerading as orthopraxy (shishtachara)...

68
00:07:01,759 --> 00:07:08,080
...were actually distorted, causing social injustices.

69
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:15,199
For example, even within the Brahmin community, unscriptural notions
of "my sub-caste is superior, yours is inferior"...

70
00:07:15,199 --> 00:07:21,120
...existed then and persist even today.

71
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:27,840
Similarly, there were incorrect assumptions about how and to what
extent other communities could serve the deity or enter the temple.

72
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:32,639
Even regarding who could perform the final rites (antima samskara)
of whom...

73
00:07:32,639 --> 00:07:37,919
...several unscriptural ideas had become common social customs.

74
00:07:37,919 --> 00:07:43,440
Only to that extent—strictly within the limits permitted
by the Shastras—did he...

75
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:50,000
...correct these deviations. That is the actual truth.
Beyond that...

76
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:55,520
...he never said that the caste system should be destroyed,
or that caste does not exist among devotees...

77
00:07:55,520 --> 00:08:01,759
...or that humanity is just one caste. On the contrary,
repeatedly in his writings...

78
00:08:01,759 --> 00:08:07,919
...he stressed that conducting oneself in accordance
with Varnashrama Dharma...

79
00:08:07,919 --> 00:08:12,960
...leads to spiritual welfare and global well-being.
Moving on to the next...

80
00:08:12,960 --> 00:08:18,000
...topic, concerning ritual discipline (Achara)...

81
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:23,840
Now, I don't see any Sri Vaishnavas here,
but there is a belief among some...

82
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:29,520
...that Ramanuja was an emotional devotee, like ISKCON followers,
completely lost in divine ecstasy...

83
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:37,839
...who forgot his daily ritual practices, and that his followers
behaved similarly. This...

84
00:08:37,839 --> 00:08:43,360
...notion is completely untrue. He was extremely rigorous
in his ritual conduct. He lived...

85
00:08:43,360 --> 00:08:48,959
...on this earth for 120 years, and even on the very last
day of his life...

86
00:08:48,959 --> 00:08:58,720
...at the age of 120, with a frail body, he went to the river
to offer Arghya-pradana...

87
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:06,160
...and only then did he cast off his mortal frame. He did not compromise...

88
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:11,279
...even a fraction of ritual discipline (Achara). Similarly, his...

89
00:09:11,279 --> 00:09:17,600
...expectations regarding the ritual conduct of others was that...

90
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:22,720
...whatever commands exist in our Shastras, the Vedas...

91
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:27,920
...the Smritis, and our respective Grihya and Dharma Sutras...

92
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:33,600
...must be regarded as the direct command of the Lord
and followed one hundred percent.

93
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:40,560
Therefore, one cannot claim to be a Sri Vaishnava in Ramanuja's lineage
merely by wearing a tilaka.

94
00:09:40,560 --> 00:09:49,120
They must perform all Vedic sacraments...

95
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:58,000
...and also undergo the five purificatory sacraments (Pancha Samskara)
described in the Pancharatra...

96
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:08,640
...including Tapa-mudra dharana (branding), Pundra (tilaka),
worship procedures, and mantras...

97
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:14,160
...and practice them regularly. This was Ramanuja's instruction.
Furthermore...

98
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:22,160
...only after doing so are they fit to be called 'Vaishnavas'...

99
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:29,760
...and not before. That was his view. Once they become Vaishnavas...

100
00:10:29,760 --> 00:10:34,880
...to be recognized as Bhagavatas, they must be Mumukshus
(seekers of liberation)...

101
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:39,600
...and exclusive, one-pointed devotees (Parama-ekantins) who have...

102
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:45,519
...offered complete surrender (Sharanagati) to Lord Vishnu.
He very systematically...

103
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:51,519
...prescribed how his followers must conduct their daily lives.

104
00:10:51,519 --> 00:10:56,160
In addition, he intended for...

105
00:10:56,160 --> 00:11:00,880
...his qualified followers to cultivate deep meditation, and
systematically...

106
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:06,240
...instructed them to study the four key texts directly from
the mouth...

107
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:13,200
...of an Acharya. Thus, even on this matter, there are
misconceptions among some...

108
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:20,720
...Sri Vaishnavas, which I have clarified here. Beyond that...

109
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:27,760
...another false notion exists that Ramanuja claimed...

110
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:33,200
...'Only through my medium or my relationship will you attain
liberation or righteousness.'

111
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:39,200
He never said this. His view was that whoever follows the truths...

112
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:45,680
...revealed in the Vedas, which he uncovered and explained, will
attain the respective fruits, be it liberation or righteousness.

113
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:53,040
Furthermore, he never claimed to be an incarnation
of Adi Shesha or Lakshmana.

114
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:58,000
That is simply the poetic exaggeration of later devotees.

115
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Another common misconception is that Ramanujas...

116
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,160
...and Sri Vaishnavas do not worship any other deity.
The truth in this is...

117
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:21,279
...that the scriptural texts and Sutras clearly mandate that daily...

118
00:12:21,279 --> 00:12:26,720
...one must offer Arghya to Surya (the sun-god) and Savitr...

119
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:33,519
...and offer portion of Vaishvadeva offerings to Rudra,
chanting 'Agnaye Svaha', 'Indraya Svaha'...

120
00:12:33,519 --> 00:12:38,240
...and perform daily Aupasana fire sacrifices and Sthalipaka rituals.

121
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:45,600
Numerous deities are addressed in these, and one must also
perform Shraddha rites...

122
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:50,720
...and offer tarpanas to the ancestors (pitrus). Whatever is
commanded in the scriptures...

123
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:56,560
...must be followed one hundred percent in our Ramanuja sampradaya.

124
00:12:56,560 --> 00:13:04,000
Therefore, within the boundaries prescribed for daily and occasional
rituals...

125
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,839
...and strictly within those limits...

126
00:13:07,839 --> 00:13:13,760
...one must worship those respective deities alongside Lord Vishnu,
as part of the ritual.

127
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:20,560
This rule is accepted by Adi Shankara and Madhvacharya as well.

128
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:28,240
There is nothing unusual about this. However, for a Parama-ekantin...

129
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:33,760
...seeking other deities beyond these prescribed duties for personal
desires is prohibited.

130
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:39,519
They must reserve supreme, singular devotion for Vishnu to be
recognized as true Vaishnavas.

131
00:13:39,519 --> 00:13:46,000
This holds true for qualified seekers; but in daily obligations,
even they...

132
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:52,240
...must make offerings to other deities as part of their obligatory
daily duties.

133
00:13:52,240 --> 00:13:58,720
This is an important clarification. Now, another...

134
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:06,160
...misconception I would like to address regarding Ramanuja—and it
often comes back to this—

135
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:14,000
...is that because of his immense emotional depth and spiritual glow...

136
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:21,600
...people assume he was purely sentimental, lacking sharp intellect
or logical reasoning.

137
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:27,040
People wonder if his logical arguments hold up, viewing him as just
a warm-hearted devotee.

138
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:35,680
But this is a complete misunderstanding. Within Vaishnavism, whether
it is Madhvas...

139
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:41,199
...ancient Gaudiya Vaishnavas, or Sri Vaishnavas, they were absolute
experts in Nyaya and Logic.

140
00:14:41,199 --> 00:14:49,040
To illustrate, whether we look at Ramanuja himself or his...

141
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:54,880
...predecessor Yamunacharya, their texts employ incredibly...

142
00:14:54,880 --> 00:15:02,399
...sharp and piercing logical arguments. Sometimes when reading them...

143
00:15:02,399 --> 00:15:07,040
...one feels pity for their opponents, thinking, 'Could they not
have spared them...

144
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:13,680
...and stopped at some point?' Such is the severity of their critique.

145
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:20,240
They raise flawless objections and expose fundamental errors.
Let me give a small example...

146
00:15:20,240 --> 00:15:27,600
...to illustrate their philosophical approach. Among modern
expositors of Vedanta...

147
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:35,040
...there is a view held by some that there is only a single Soul
(Ekatma-vada)...

148
00:15:35,040 --> 00:15:39,600
...that there is no difference between my soul and your soul.

149
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:48,320
They claim 'I am the Supreme Self without any difference, and perceived
duality is just ignorance'.

150
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:57,040
In his commentary on the Bhagavad Gita, Ramanuja addresses this
directly, asking:

151
00:15:57,040 --> 00:16:04,560
'Do you truly believe in this theory of a single soul? Are you
established in it?'

152
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:09,839
There can only be two answers: 'Yes, I am fully established in it'...'

153
00:16:09,839 --> 00:16:15,759
...or, 'No, I don't really believe it, I am just saying it for the
sake of it'.

154
00:16:15,759 --> 00:16:22,320
If you choose the second option—that you do not genuinely believe it—

155
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:30,320
Ramanuja asks: 'If you yourself do not believe it, why preach it
to others?'

156
00:16:30,320 --> 00:16:35,839
'Why write hundreds of books about it? Why establish monasteries?'

157
00:16:35,839 --> 00:16:41,040
This shows a contradiction. Now, let's consider the first option:

158
00:16:41,040 --> 00:16:48,320
If you are indeed fully established in the belief of a single soul...

159
00:16:48,320 --> 00:16:54,639
...then the person you are teaching is not different from you.

160
00:16:54,639 --> 00:17:02,560
If a person stands before a mirror and starts lecturing his own
reflection...

161
00:17:02,560 --> 00:17:08,400
...we would call that person insane, wouldn't we?

162
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:14,640
Therefore, if you believe in a single soul, lecturing others...

163
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:22,640
...writing books, and establishing monasteries is completely
illogical.

164
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:27,120
It contradicts your own philosophical stance. Thus, both options
fail.

165
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:33,600
Through such powerful dialectics, they expose logical flaws on
various subjects.

166
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:38,799
This showcases their exceptional command over logic and analysis.

167
00:17:38,799 --> 00:17:45,280
Now, let us examine another misconception...

168
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:51,440
...which is that they only engaged in refuting others.
In reality, they did so as a service to God.

169
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:57,200
We must understand that their intellectual endeavors...

170
00:17:57,200 --> 00:18:03,760
...flowed directly from their profound experience of the Soul and
the Divine...

171
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:09,760
...which manifested in various ways. Another major misconception is that...

172
00:18:09,760 --> 00:18:17,280
...the Vaishnava tradition is a modern invention, conceived by
Ramanuja and his immediate predecessors...

173
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:24,000
...and that before them, Vaishnavism and devotion (bhakti) did not
exist in the Vedic fold.

174
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:28,799
This is a complete historical error. Why?

175
00:18:28,799 --> 00:18:35,280
If we look at it from a scientific, historical perspective...

176
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:42,400
...the Vedas date back to at least 5,000 years ago.

177
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:46,960
And even in the Rigveda—the oldest Vedic text—

178
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:53,200
...whose earliest mandalas contain mentions of...

179
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:58,000
...Indra, Mitra, Varuna, Vishnu, and Rudra...

180
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:05,200
...although some argue Vishnu's supremacy is not as dominant there.

181
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:12,320
Scholars call the Rigveda's style the Hautra tradition...

182
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:19,679
...which is primarily connected with the Hotr priest. Later,
the Adhvaryava tradition...

183
00:19:19,679 --> 00:19:24,960
...rose to prominence in the Kuru-Panchala region.

184
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:33,440
This brought the Yajurveda forward, which proclaims: Yajño vai
Viṣṇuḥ (Sacrifice is Vishnu).

185
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:38,000
The Aitareya Brahmana, belonging to that historical era, declares...

186
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:46,559
...Agnir vai devānām avamo, Viṣṇuḥ paramaḥ (Agni is the lowest of gods,
Vishnu is the highest) [1].

187
00:19:46,559 --> 00:19:52,559
Similarly, the Vaikhanasa school, linked to the Taittiriya branch...

188
00:19:52,559 --> 00:19:58,240
...of the Krishna Yajurveda, contains the highly ancient Vaikhanasa
Sutras.

189
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:06,000
These are cited in the Baudhayana Sutras and other early texts.

190
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:11,520
The Vaikhanasa Sutras and their associated mantra texts...

191
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:18,080
...are as old as the Yajurveda, clearly demonstrating the ancient
nature of Vaishnavism.

192
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:24,559
It represents an orthodox Vedic path. Similarly, roots of
the Pancharatra...

193
00:20:24,559 --> 00:20:30,880
...can be traced to the Shukla Yajurveda, proving its deep antiquity.

194
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:36,240
Furthermore, archaeological evidence, such as ancient inscriptions...

195
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:41,919
...includes the famous Heliodorus Pillar, erected when successors
of Alexander...

196
00:20:41,919 --> 00:20:48,880
...invaded. It records that Greek (Yavana) ambassadors became
devotees of Vishnu...

197
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:53,120
...and built monuments in His honor. Hence, Vaishnavism is highly
ancient.

198
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:59,679
The Pancharatra system is also described in the Narayaniya section
of the Mahabharata.

199
00:20:59,679 --> 00:21:05,360
Thus, its antiquity is fully established.

200
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:11,200
Moreover, in later periods...

201
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:16,480
...the Dravida Divya Prabandhams arose, particularly in Tamil Nadu...

202
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:22,960
...dating back around 1,500 years. The earlier Vedic roots go back
2,500 to 4,000 years.

203
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:32,159
The systems I mentioned earlier are ancient, and the Tamil hymns
date back 1,500 years.

204
